ual proof, and a release recommendation. Never mark an incomplete or failed candidate ready and never rerun a failed worker automatically. If one book fails, preserve its phase/log and complete independent work on the others without claiming the collection is synchronized.\n\nAudit that all four books used the same cutoff and frozen evidence, every shared update has four justified dispositions, shared claims agree, and protected file hashes remain unchanged. Advance the shared research checkpoint only after the complete four-book audit passes. Return one collection report with each book's status, exact changes and why they are warranted with direct primary-source links, candidate and evidence links, version recommendations, limitations, synchronization result, and protected-file result. An unchanged book still needs a completed evidence review. Do not commit, push, merge, publish, deploy, replace production files, send messages to others, launch a nested Codex process, or start another scheduled run. Report the completion, failure, or required review decision to Mike."
